details:
(a) whether any proposal has been received from the State Government for renovation of the dilapidated road that passes through the forest land between Salur and Agatheeswaramangalam road which has been used by the people for a long time in Thirukkazhukundram Panchayat Union,Chengalpattu district,Tamil Nadu;
(b) whether any technical observations or additional documents have been sought from the State Government or the implementing agency for processing the proposal;
(c) if so, the reasons for pendency of the proposal, if any; and
(d) the likely time-frame for completion of scrutiny and communication of the final decision?

(a) whether Government has assessed the changing weather patterns, coastal vulnerabilities and risks arising from climate change in Gujarat, Maharashtra and Tamil Nadu;
(b) the details regarding coverage provided by weather monitoring, Doppler radar and early warning systems in these States;
(c) the manner in which scientific data generated by national meteorological and oceanographic agencies is being utilized for disaster preparedness and mitigation;
(d) whether Government proposes to strengthen climate resilience and forecasting capabilities in these States; and
(e) the details of major weather and ocean observation facilities operating in these States?

(a) the status of tribal-development programmes and infrastructure available in tribal habitations in the State of Tamil Nadu;
(b) the measures undertaken by Government to improve access to education, healthcare, livelihoods and connectivity for tribal communities in the State;
(c) the assessment made regarding socio-economic conditions and development indicators among tribal populations in the State;
(d) the initiatives proposed to be taken for preserving tribal culture while promoting inclusive development in the State; and
(e) the district-wise details of tribal beneficiaries covered under major schemes in the State during the last three years?

(a) the initiatives undertaken to address the impact of rising global prices of phosphatic fertilizers on farmers in Tamil Nadu;
(b) the measures implemented to ensure adequate availability of Diammonium Phosphate (DAP) and other phosphatic fertilizers during agricultural seasons in the State;
(c) the arrangements put in place for supporting fertilizer supply chains, including import-related and production-related interventions;
(d) the efforts made to coordinate with domestic producers and international suppliers to maintain stable fertilizer availability; and
(e) the outcomes achieved in ensuring affordable prices, adequate supply and timely access to fertilizers in Tamil Nadu?

(a) whether Government has taken cognizance of the difficulties faced by business class passengers, including senior citizens, dignitaries and VVIPs, in accessing feeder buses at airports where aircraft are parked at remote bays;
(b) if so, the details of complaints received by Government regarding inadequate seating and overcrowding in such buses;
(c) the measures proposed to be taken by Government to introduce separate feeder buses for premium passengers at airports across the country;
(d) the airports where such facilities are presently available; and
(e) the timeline for wider implementation of this arrangement?

(a) whether Government is aware that the railway level crossing near Melavalampettai on the Thirukazhukundram–Madurantakam Karunguzhi Road in Chengalpattu District, Tamil Nadu, serves as an important link connecting Mahabalipuram with GST Road, provides access to Old Mahabalipuram Road and East Coast Road, and functions as a bypass route to Chennai;
(b) whether Government has received any proposal for constructing a Road over Bridge (RoB) at the above railway level crossing;
(c) whether the feasibility of the project has been examined; and
(d) present status, estimated cost and time frame for execution of the proposed RoB?

(a) whether telecom connectivity gaps continue to persist in certain parts of Tamil Nadu, particularly in remote and coastal regions;
(b) the extent of mobile and broadband infrastructure expanded under Government-supported programmes in the State;
(c) the findings available with Government regarding quality of telecom services and internet accessibility in the State;
(d) the roadmap prepared for improving digital connectivity and communication networks across the State; and
(e) the district-wise progress achieved under major telecom infrastructure projects in the State?

(a) Government's assessment of food-security and consumer-protection mechanisms operating in the State of Tamil Nadu and their effectiveness in reaching beneficiaries;
(b) the measures undertaken for improving transparency, digitisation and efficiency of the Public Distribution System in the State;
(c) the major challenges affecting distribution of essential commodities and consumer grievance redressal in the State;
(d) the initiatives proposed to be taken for strengthening food-security delivery and consumer-awareness programmes in the State; and
(e) the district-wise number of beneficiaries covered under food-security schemes in the State during the last three years?

(a) the factors underlying the estimated Gross Domestic Product (GDP) growth of about 7.7 per cent during 2025-26 and the extent to which such growth was broad-based across sectors;
(b) the implications of rising crude oil prices, developments in West Asia, global trade uncertainties and inflationary pressures for economic growth;
(c) the sectors considered most vulnerable to external shocks and the safeguards created to enhance economic resilience;
(d) the role expected from consumption, infrastructure spending, manufacturing and private investment in sustaining growth; and
(e) the policy approach proposed for balancing growth, fiscal discipline and price stability?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the increasing electricity requirements of the country arising from economic growth, urbanisation, rising temperatures and expanding domestic consumption patterns;
(b) the status of systems established for maintaining grid stability, forecasting demand patterns and coordinating power availability among generating, transmission and distribution entities;
(c) the extent to which additions in generation capacity, transmission infrastructure and renewable energy resources have strengthened reliability of electricity supply across the country; and
(d) the measures proposed to be taken by Government to address future peak demand requirements and ensure adequate, affordable and reliable power availability for all consumers?

(a) the concerns brought to the notice of Government regarding water scarcity in drought-prone regions of the State of Tamil Nadu and the need for expansion of rainwater-harvesting structures;
(b) the assistance provided for Panchayat-level implementation, community participation, technical training and monitoring of rain water-harvesting initiatives in the State;
(c) the measures proposed by Government to integrate rainwater harvesting with groundwater recharge and sustainable water-resource management practices; and
(d) the outcomes achieved in strengthening water security, protecting livelihoods and enhancing resilience to climate-related water stress in the State of Tamil Nadu?

(a) the objectives underlying the Viksit Bharat-Guarantee for Rozgar and Ajeevika Mission (Gramin) (VB-G RAM G) Act, 2025 and the manner in which the government proposes to strengthen rural employment and livelihood opportunities through the new framework;
(b) the employment guarantees, livelihood support measures and coverage envisaged for rural households under the VB-G RAM G Act, 2025;
(c) the changes introduced in funding arrangements, implementation mechanisms and worker entitlements as compared to the earlier rural employment guarantee framework; and 
(d) the monitoring, evaluation and grievance redressal systems established by Government to ensure effective implementation and benefits for vulnerable rural workers?

(a) the present status of 500 MWe Prototype Fast Breeder Reactor (PFBR) at Kalpakkam in Tamil Nadu following the achievement of first criticality;
(b) the measures undertaken by Government to facilitate commissioning activities, safety validation and regulatory clearances associated with the project;
(c) the observations of Government regarding the contribution of PFBR technology to the second stage of the country's three-stage nuclear programme; and
(d) the initiatives proposed to be taken for ensuring timely commencement of commercial power generation from the facility?

(a) the present status of healthcare infrastructure and service-delivery systems in Tamil Nadu, including primary, secondary and tertiary healthcare facilities;
(b) the measures undertaken by Government to strengthen healthcare access, disease surveillance and medical infrastructure in the State;
(c) the major public-health challenges identified in the State and the action taken thereon;
(d) the initiatives proposed to be taken for improving healthcare outcomes, medical manpower and quality of healthcare services in the State; and
(e) the allocation and utilisation of central assistance under major health programmes in the State during the last three years, district-wise?

(a) the status of metro rail utilisation in the State of Tamil Nadu, particularly Chennai, in comparison with projected passenger demand and investment in metro infrastructure;
(b) the extent to which urban transport policies have contributed to development of metro systems, bus services and non-motorised transport networks in the State of Tamil Nadu; and
(c) the measures proposed to be taken by the Central Government to strengthen integrated urban mobility, improve public transport usage and enhance connectivity with metro systems in the State?

(a) the changes brought about in Tamil Nadu through major rural development programmes relating to livelihoods, housing and infrastructure creation;
(b) the utilisation pattern of resources provided under key rural development schemes in the State;
(c) the progress recorded in employment generation, connectivity and creation of rural assets;
(d) the contribution of such interventions towards strengthening livelihoods and self-employment opportunities; and
(e) the strategy being pursued for improving development outcomes in rural Tamil Nadu?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the compliance of occupational safety standards in hazardous industrial establishments in Tiruvallur district, Tamil Nadu following the recent ammonia gas leak that caused fatalities and injuries among migrant workers;
(b) the details of inspections, prosecutions and penalties initiated by Government against industries handling hazardous substances;
(c) whether periodic third-party safety audits, emergency evacuation drills, and multilingual safety training are proposed for hazardous industries;
(d) the details of compensation and rehabilitation provided to the affected workers and their families; and
(e) the details of steps proposed to strengthen industrial safety enforcement and employer accountability?

(a) the observations of Government regarding regional and socio-economic disparities affecting vulnerable communities in Tamil Nadu;
(b) the measures undertaken to improve access to education, skill development and financial assistance for disadvantaged sections in the State;
(c) the progress achieved through scholarship, rehabilitation and empowerment programmes implemented in the State;
(d) the initiatives proposed to be taken for enhancing social mobility and economic participation among beneficiary groups in the State; and
(e) the district-wise allocation and utilisation of funds under major welfare programmes in the State during the last three years?

(a) status of welfare and empowerment programmes implemented for Scheduled Castes, Other Backward Classes, senior citizens and Persons with Disabilities (PwDs) in Tamil Nadu;
(b) measures undertaken by Government to improve educational, economic and social outcomes among beneficiary groups in the State;
(c) assessment made regarding the effectiveness of ongoing social-justice interventions and welfare schemes in the State;
(d) initiatives proposed to be taken for strengthening social inclusion, accessibility and livelihood opportunities in the State; and
(e) category-wise number of beneficiaries covered under major schemes in the State during the last three years?

(a) whether Government has received any representation for opening a nationalised bank branch at Perumarudhur Panchayat in Manamelkudi Taluk, Pudukkottai District, Tamil Nadu;
(b) the norms governing branch expansion in rural areas;
(c) whether banking requirements of these villages have been assessed;
(d) whether hardships faced by residents have been examined; and
(e) the action proposed to establish a Public Sector Bank (PSB) branch in the area?

(a) whether Government has reviewed safety protocols governing the storage, transportation and handling of ammonia and other hazardous chemicals following the Ammonia gas leak in Tiruvallur district, Tamil Nadu;
(b) the details of safety standards prescribed for refrigeration systems using ammonia and the mechanism for ensuring compliance;
(c) whether mandatory installation of ammonia leak detectors, automatic alarm systems and real-time monitoring equipment is under consideration;
(d) the gaps identified in enforcement of existing safety regulations; and
(e) the action proposed to prevent recurrence of similar industrial disasters across the country?
J

(a) whether Government has undertaken any review of urban flood management and storm-water infrastructure in Chennai and other major cities of the State of Tamil Nadu;
(b) the details of projects supported by the Central Government for flood mitigation, urban drainage improvement and water conservation;
(c) the progress achieved in integrating storm-water systems with groundwater recharge and water-body restoration initiatives;
(d) whether recurring urban flooding has revealed deficiencies in existing infrastructure; and
(e) the measures proposed to enhance climate resilience and flood preparedness in the State of Tamil Nadu, urban centres?

(a) whether Government has assessed the adequacy of ?30,000 crore budget allocation for Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme (MGNREGS) in 2026–27 in meeting rural employment demand amid uneven rural recovery;
(b) the details of demand projections, employment trends and State-wise utilisation patterns taken into account by Government while determining this allocation; and
(c) the measures proposed to be taken by Government to ensure timely wage payments, creation of durable assets, effective grievance redressal and transparency in programme implementation?

(a) whether Government has examined the vulnerability of export-oriented sectors to disruptions in shipping lanes arising from the ongoing Iran–Israel conflict and the wider West Asia crisis impacting maritime trade routes such as the Strait of Hormuz;
(b) if so, the details of sectoral risk assessments undertaken by Government covering Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) and export-intensive industries affected by shipping disruptions linked to the Iran–Israel war; and
(c) the policy measures proposed to be taken by Government to protect Indian exporters from prolonged trade route disruptions arising from the Iran–Israel conflict and associated maritime instability?

(a) whether Government has examined concerns that many students born and raised in Tamil Nadu face academic barriers in Kendriya Vidyalayas where Tamil is not the medium of instruction;
(b) if so, the details of consultations held by Government with parents, students and State authorities; and
(c) the steps proposed to be taken by Government to address medium-of-instruction concerns and improve inclusivity for regional language learners in Kendriya Vidyalayas?

(a) whether Government has examined the regulatory and safety framework of the Atomic Energy Regulatory Board (AERB) and other statutory bodies to ensure that NTPC’s nuclear projects meet national and international safety standards;
(b) if so, the details of specific protocols, periodic inspection mechanisms and compliance benchmarks set by Government for emerging nuclear projects; and
(c) the details of Government's planned outreach to local communities, States hosting nuclear sites and educational institutions to promote awareness, training and local economic participation in nuclear energy deployment?

(a) whether Government has developed or is planning to develop targeted programmes to equip youth with practical skills in emerging fields such as Artificial Intelligence (AI), robotics and biotechnologies;
(b) if so, the details of the funding, institutional partnerships and certifications available under these programmes for students; and
(c) the timeframe Government envisages for broad roll-out of such skill enhancement initiatives in schools and higher-education institutions nationwide?

(a) whether Government has examined the proposal for construction of a public flyover across the railway line connecting the East Coast Road to Vandavasi near Melmaruvathur in Chengalpattu district, Tamil Nadu;
(b) if so, the details of surveys, approvals and coordination undertaken by Government with the State Government for execution of the project, including funding pattern and present status; and
(c) the timeline estimated by Government for expediting construction of the flyover and expected completion period, along with reasons in case the project has not progressed as anticipated?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the calls for reforming the Indian Forest Service (IFS) to align its mandate with 21st-century environmental challenges, including water security, climate resilience, biodiversity conservation and ecosystem services, beyond its traditional colonial-era policing role;
(b) if so, the details of assessments made by Government on expanding the role and responsibilities of IFS Officers in ecological outcomes such as groundwater recharge and forest stream revival; and
(c) the action plan proposed by Government to modernise the forest service’s framework?

(a) whether Government is aware of reports highlighting disparities in educational and digital infrastructure between urban and rural schools;
(b) the initiatives being undertaken to ensure equitable digital access in rural areas;
(c) whether programmes have been launched to improve rural school infrastructure, such as classrooms, libraries, sanitation and laboratories and the funds allocated;
(d) the availability of qualified teachers in rural schools vis-à-vis urban schools;
(e) whether incentives are planned to encourage teacher postings in rural areas; and
(f) whether a roadmap exists to monitor and reduce dropout rates, especially among rural girl students?

(a) whether Government is aware of the lack of dialysis facilities for chronic kidney disease patients in rural and semi-urban areas of Tamil Nadu;
(b) the number of Primary Health Centres (PHCs) in the State equipped with dialysis facilities, district-wise;
(c) whether any assessment has been undertaken regarding the adequacy of dialysis infrastructure, manpower, and maintenance at PHCs;
(d) the funds allocated and utilised under the National Health Mission (NHM) or other Central schemes for this purpose during the last three years; and
(e) the steps taken or proposed to expand affordable dialysis services at the primary healthcare level for economically weaker sections?

(a) whether Government support and welfare measures for aviation personnel working in the State of Tamil Nadu airports to ensure healthcare, housing and livelihood opportunities;
(b) the schemes implemented for medical facilities at airports Authority of India residential colonies in Chennai, housing support for staff attached to Madurai airport and training programmes at Coimbatore airport to strengthen the delivery of welfare initiatives; and
(c) Government’s plans to expand grievance redressal systems for airport staff, improve monitoring of welfare projects across Tiruchirappalli and Salem and integrate personnel welfare measures into social security frameworks for aviation workers in the State of Tamil Nadu?

(a) whether Government has examined the rapid expansion of Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies in 2025 across creative, educational, professional and social domains, including AI-generated content and AI-assisted decision-making and the implications of such dependence;
(b) if so, the details of assessments undertaken by Government on risks related to human cognition, misinformation and impacts on indigenous creative sectors; and
(c) the measures proposed by Government to promote responsible AI adoption while safeguarding human intellectual capacity and cultural creativity?

(a) whether Government has examined international best practices in tariff policy and automotive export-led growth, drawing lessons from countries with low tariffs and strong intra-industry trade participation such as Germany, South Korea and China;
(b) if so, the details of comparative analysis undertaken by Government on policy frameworks, technology transfer and supply-chain integration relevant to India’s automotive exports;
(c) the policy actions proposed by Government to rationalise tariff structures, strengthen trade negotiations and improve the global competitiveness of India’s automotive manufacturing and export sector?

(a) whether Government has taken note of Article 130 of the Constitution enabling the Supreme Court to sit at places other than New Delhi with the President’s approval and whether Government has assessed regional sittings;
(b) if so, the details of proposals or representations received by Government during the last five years seeking Supreme Court benches or sittings in southern India, including Tamil Nadu, Kerala, Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh and Puducherry; and
(c) the steps proposed to be taken by Government for examining such proposals with constitutional authorities and disclosing the status of consideration?

(a) whether Government has examined how AI reduces entry-level opportunities for graduates and increases the need for Government-supported internship pathways;
(b) if so, the details of Government measures aligning internship training with AI-driven industry needs and preparing youth for roles beyond traditional entry-level jobs; and
(c) what actions Government proposes for collaboration with industry, academia and start-ups to ensure interns transition into productive employment pathways?

(a) whether Government is aware of the resurfacing of toxic froth at the Yamuna ghat in Kalindi Kunj, rendering stretches of the river nearly invisible and posing serious risks to public health and ecology;
(b) the reasons for its recurring occurrence, including untreated sewage, industrial effluents and detergent-laden discharges;
(c) the steps taken under the Yamuna Action Plan and related programmes to improve water quality in this stretch;
(d) whether accountability has been fixed on agencies or local bodies violating discharge norms; and
(e) the additional measures with timelines proposed for effective sewage treatment, monitoring and long-term ecological restoration of the Yamuna river?

(a) whether the DGCA has completed its investigation into the recent tail-strike incident involving an IndiGo aircraft at Chennai International airport;
(b) if so, the key findings of the investigation and the identified causes of the incident;
(c) details of the remedial or corrective actions that have been directed to be carried out by the airline and airport authorities; and
(d) the measures that are being implemented to ensure continued safety and prevent recurrence of such incidents at the Chennai aviation hub?

(a) whether Government has examined the long-standing demand to permit conduct of court proceedings in Tamil, particularly in the High Courts and subordinate courts of Tamil Nadu, in order to improve access to justice for litigants, witnesses and advocates who are more conversant with the Tamil language;
(b) if so, the details and present status thereof; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has examined the importance of research-based learning methodologies and the development of soft skills, such as communication, teamwork, critical thinking and problem-solving for students' employability, global readiness and personal growth;
(b) if so, the details of policy initiatives and educational reforms introduced by Government to integrate research-oriented learning, experimental learning and soft skill development into school, college and higher education circuits to align academic outcomes with industry expectations; and
(c) the strategic framework proposed by Government to ensure that students are better prepared for complex real-world challenges and employment opportunities in a competitive global environment?

(a) whether Government has evaluated how academic institutions' curricula and teaching methods are aligning with evolving industry demands that prioritise skills, adaptability and practical exposure over formal degrees alone;
(b) if so, the details of specific reforms proposed to integrate work-based learning, project portfolios and AI-relevant competencies into campus programmes; and
(c) the time frame envisaged by Government for rolling out such a curriculum and employability enhancement reforms nationwide?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to ensure effective utilisation of funds allocated under the Menstrual Hygiene Scheme across States, including the State of Tamil Nadu;
(b) if so, the details of measures taken for strengthening sanitary napkin procurement and distribution in Tamil Nadu, along with the reach of Jan Aushadhi Suvidha Pads; and
(c) whether Government proposes to expand coordination with State Governments and local bodies to improve awareness campaigns and equitable access to menstrual hygiene services?

(a) whether Government has examined the impact of frequent food price volatility on household nutrition and consumption patterns;
(b) whether Government has evaluated the adequacy of buffer stocks and market intervention mechanisms; and
(c) whether Government proposes reforms to improve price stabilisation while protecting both producers and consumers?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the status of airport infrastructure across the State of Tamil Nadu, including passenger convenience, safety and operational efficiency;
(b) the measures adopted to expand Chennai International airport with new integrated terminals, modernise Coimbatore International airport with advanced baggage and security systems and upgrade Madurai and Tiruchirappalli airports with improved runways, lounges and cargo facilities to meet rising demand; and
(c) the steps proposed to strengthen digital ticketing, grievance redressal platforms and real-time monitoring systems at Salem airport and other regional airports to ensure sustainable aviation growth in the State of Tamil Nadu?

(a) whether Government has evaluated the preparedness of India's labour regulatory framework in addressing job displacement risks arising from advanced automation and artificial intelligence adoption within corporate and service sectors;
(b) if so, the details of institutional mechanisms and expert consultations initiated by Government for workforce protection; and
(c) the steps proposed by Government to align labour laws, social security coverage and employment safety nets with emerging technological realities?

(a) whether Government has examined the implications of evolving trade relations with the United States, including tariff pressures and commercial disputes affecting Indian exports, for India's broader foreign policy and economic diplomacy;
(b) if so, the details of assessments made by Government of tariff-linked risks and strategic responses formulated to safeguard India's export competitiveness; and
(c) the diplomatic and economic measures proposed to be taken by Government to strengthen India-US trade ties while protecting national interests?

(a) whether the Ministry is aware that there is an order to give priority to local people in employment at Kalpakkam;
(b) whether the said order is currently in force and the number of persons provided employment during the last five years; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether the Ministry is aware that the work on National Highway NH-332A, connecting Mamallapuram and Puducherry, has been facing significant delays in execution;
(b) the present status of the project, including the percentage of work completed so far; and
(c) the reasons for the delay in construction and whether the Ministry has set a revised timeline for completion of NH-332A?

(a) Government’s ongoing schemes aimed at improving women’s health, including maternal and adolescent nutrition programmes;
(b) Government’s efforts to tackle anemia and reproductive health issues among women through enhanced medical infrastructure and awareness; and
(c) the digital and telemedicine initiatives introduced by Government to provide accessible healthcare services to women in rural and remote areas?

(a) the steps taken or proposed to be taken by Government to increase production and blending of biofuels such as ethanol and Compressed Biogas (CBG), particularly from non-food sources such as agricultural and municipal waste;
(b) the current status of the Ethanol Blending Programme (EBP) in terms of percentage blending achieved so far and the targets set for the next three years, year-wise; and
(c) the initiatives undertaken by Government to encourage rapid commissioning and scaling up of second-generation ethanol plants and commercial CBG plants, including any incentives or financial support mechanisms?

(a) whether Government has taken initiative to bridge the educational gap, promote inclusive learning across urban, rural areas for equitable education access in the country;
(b) if so, the details of Government's initiative, including programmes, infrastructure development, teaching training and policies to ensure equitable education access for all students nationwide; and 
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government concurs with the view that India should aim to become a global design and manufacturing hub for industrial electronics, not just a user, to drive technological self-reliance and economic growth;
(b) if so, the details of the initiatives that are proposed to be taken by Government to leverage industrial electronics for smart factories, robotics, intelligent grids, automated transport systems, through technological advancements, policy support, and international collaborations; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the initiatives taken by Government to strengthen environmental sustainability and ecological balance in Tamil Nadu;
(b) the programmes launched by Government for climate resilience and disaster management in the State; and
(c) the plans of Government to involve local communities in conservation efforts and increase awareness regarding environmental protection?

(a) whether Government is aware of significant contribution of stubble burning to air pollution in various parts of the country;
(b) the steps taken or proposed to be taken by Government to promote alternatives for stubble disposal among farmers; and
(c) details of financial/technical support provided by Government for crop residue management with a view to reducing incidents of stubble burning?

(a) whether Government has made progress towards achieving gender equality, empowerment of women, improving access to education, health services and economic opportunities;
(b) if so, the details of the steps that have been taken by Government to remove barriers to women's economic, civic participation, access to services and leadership roles nationwide; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the present condition of school infrastructure in rural areas, including availability of toilets, classrooms and digital facilities;
(b) Government's plan to bridge the digital divide exposed by the pandemic; and 
(c) the initiatives undertaken by Government to create supportive environments that empower teachers and foster innovative learning?

(a) the Government's current strategies and programmes to reduce the prevalence of chronic diseases such as diabetes and heart conditions across the country;
(b) Government's efforts to enhance adult vaccination coverage and lower vaccine-preventable diseases across all age groups; and
(c) the Measures Government is implementing to improve health care infrastructure including access to medical facilities and affordable health care services nationwide?

(a) whether the ethanol blending programme has led to increased demand for food crops like maize and sugarcane, thereby raising serious concerns over food security, water usage, and the livelihoods of other farmers;
(b) the steps Government proposes to take to balance ethanol production with agricultural sustainability and to prevent any adverse impact on food prices and availability; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?
